.TH BEEMR 1 2026-10-03 "beemr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
beemr \- peer\-to\-peer file and message sharing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beemr share
.I path
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR device ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR count ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-upnp ]
.br
.B beemr get
.I ticket
.RB [ \-o
.IR folder ]
.br
.B beemr msg
.I contact\-or\-id message
.br
.B beemr inbox
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.br
.B beemr reply
.I number message
.br
.B beemr
.RB { setup | id | name | contact | daemon | relay | doctor | help | version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beemr
sends files and messages straight to another device, with no servers,
accounts or setup.
It connects directly when it can (same network, IPv6, or a port opened on the
router with UPnP), punches through NATs when it can't, and falls back to
relaying through other beemr devices.
Devices find each other through signed records on the BitTorrent Mainline DHT.
All traffic is end\-to\-end encrypted.
.PP
Every device has a cryptographic identity, created on first use, and a name
chosen by its user.
Names of devices that are not saved as contacts are shown as unverified.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "share " path
Share a file or folder and print a
.B beemr get
command for the other device.
By default the share allows one download and never expires.
.TP
.BI "get " ticket
Download a share into the current folder, or the folder given with
.BR \-o .
Files are saved under a free name and are never overwritten.
.TP
.BI "msg " "contact\-or\-id message"
Send a text message.
If the other device can't be reached, the message is queued and delivered
automatically by the background service.
.TP
.B inbox
Show received messages, newest first, and mark them read.
.TP
.BI "reply " "number message"
Reply to a message in the inbox.
.TP
.B setup
Name this device and start the background service, which receives messages.
.TP
.B id
Print this device's ID, which others use to reach it.
.TP
.BR name " [" \fInew\ name\fR ]
Show or change this device's name.
.TP
.BR contact " {" add " \fIname id\fR | " list " | " remove " \fIname\fR}"
Manage saved contacts.
.TP
.BR daemon " {" status | install | uninstall | run }
Manage the background service.
.B status
exits with status 3 when the service is not running.
.TP
.BR relay " {" run " [" \-\-private "] [" \-\-port " \fIport\fR] | " use " \fIaddress\fR | " list " | " remove " \fIaddress\fR}"
Run a relay for devices that can't connect directly, or configure relays to use.
.TP
.B doctor
Report how reachable this device is: local network, IPv6, UPnP, direct
reachability, hole punching and relays.
.SH SHARE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-to " contact\-or\-id"
Only this device may download.
Repeat for several devices.
.TP
.BI "\-n, \-\-downloads " count
Number of downloads to allow (default 1; 0 means unlimited).
.TP
.BI "\-e, \-\-expires " time
Stop accepting downloads after a time such as 30s, 10m, 2h or 1d.
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-port " port
Listen on this TCP and UDP port instead of a random one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-upnp
Don't ask the router to open a port.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BEEMR_HOME
Folder for the identity, contacts and inbox (default
.I ~/.config/beemr
on Linux).
.TP
.B BEEMR_LOG
Diagnostic logging, for example
.BR BEEMR_LOG=debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/beemr/identity
This device's private key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/beemr/contacts
Saved contacts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/beemr/inbox.jsonl
Received messages.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
beemr share photos/ \-n 3 \-e 2h
beemr share contract.pdf \-\-to sara
beemr get <ticket> \-o ~/Downloads
beemr contact add Sara <device\-id>
beemr msg sara "are you free tonight?"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/osmanahmadxai/beemr
